---
description: DefenseScene is a thin coordinator; don't grow it or bypass NightResult
globs:
  - src/scenes/DefenseScene.ts
  - src/scenes/defense/**/*.ts
  - src/scenes/defenseNightLogic.ts
alwaysApply: false
---

- `DefenseScene` orchestrates modules under `src/scenes/defense/`. Put new night-loop behavior there, not as more methods on the scene class.
- Already split: WorldBootstrap, HudController, WaveSpawner, EnemySpawner, EnemyTick, ProjectileTick, NightEnd, Targeting, SpellDirector, SpellWorldTick, PlayerCombat, GroundAim, DebugDraw, EndlessSpawn, RunSetup, SceneLifecycle, SceneE2E, defenseGroundAimInput. Extend these; don't re-extract them.
- Never mutate town/save rules from the scene. End a night through the night-end module and a `NightResult`.
- E2E hooks are `scene.e2e.*` (`DefenseSceneE2EHost.ts` binds every `defenseSceneE2e*` helper). Add a helper to `DefenseSceneE2E{Combat,Obstacles,Hud}.ts`; don't add `e2e*` methods to the scene.
- `@internal until X module lands` comments are stale once the module exists.
- `DefenseSpellDirector` keeps the queue/auto-cast/cast-start logic; channel ticks live in `DefenseSpellChannel.ts`, telegraphs/heal FX in `DefenseSpellTelegraphs.ts`, effect resolution/blink/ice wall in `DefenseSpellResolve.ts`.
